## Architettura (schema del progetto)

### High-level

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    UI[Frontend\nNext.js :3000] -->|HTTP JSON| API[Backend\nFastAPI :8000]
    API -->|SQLAlchemy| DB[(Postgres :5432)]

    API -->|background poller| SIM[Inbox Simulator\n(tickets/ samples)]
    SIM -->|"new email"| API

    API -->|invoke| LG[LangGraph\nIngest Email Engine]
    LG -->|categorize + draft| LLM[Anthropic Messages API]
    LG -->|enrich (mock)| ENR1[Mock Sentry]
    LG -->|enrich (DB)| ENR2[mock_customers]

    LG -->|final_state| API
    API -->|persist| DB

    LG --> LOG[backend/logs/ingest_pipeline.log]
```

### Struttura repo

```text
.
├─ docker-compose.yml
├─ README
├─ backend/
│  ├─ main.py
│  ├─ database.py
│  └─ ingest_email_engine/
│     ├─ graph.py
│     ├─ state.py
│     ├─ llm.py
│     ├─ logger.py
│     └─ nodes/
├─ frontend/
│  └─ src/app/page.tsx
├─ tickets/                 # dataset sample (ticket_*.txt)
└─ materials/               # immagini per documentazione
```

## Setup (Docker - consigliato)

### Prerequisiti

- Docker Desktop (con `docker compose`)

### 1) Configura variabili ambiente

Crea/edita un file `.env` nella root (non committare chiavi):

```dotenv
# LLM (Anthropic)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-3-haiku-20240307

# Postgres (opzionale; se vuoti usa i default del compose)
POSTGRES_USER=admin
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=password123
POSTGRES_DB=support_db
```

### 2) Avvia lo stack

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Servizi:

- Frontend: [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)
- Backend API: [http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000)
- Postgres: localhost:5432

### 3) Genera ticket (inbox simulator)

Da UI:

- premi **Start** per avviare la simulazione inbox
- vedrai comparire nuovi ticket secondo l’intervallo configurato

Oppure via API:

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/simulation/start
# Support Ticketing MVP (Inbox Simulator + AI Triage)

End-to-end MVP that simulates an email inbox, turns “emails” into tickets, enriches/triages them through a **LangGraph** pipeline, persists everything to **Postgres**, and renders it in a **Next.js** dashboard.

![User Interface](materials/user%20interface.jpeg)

## VERY IMPORTANT DISCLAIMER (Inbox/Email Simulation)

This project is **NOT** connected to a real Outlook/Gmail inbox and it does **NOT** send real emails.

- **Simulated inbox**: incoming emails are produced by a background **poller** that picks local samples from `tickets/ticket_*.txt` (or falls back to an internal mock set).
- **Sample data**: the dataset is anonymized/tagged and used only to simulate support requests.
- **“Outlook thread parity” is demonstrational**: when you reply from the UI, the backend prepares an email with `In-Reply-To` and `References` headers (like Outlook threading), but **SMTP sending is disabled** for safety (local MVP).
- **No authentication**: admin/simulation endpoints are open because this is a local MVP.

A real integration would require IMAP/SMTP or Microsoft Graph (plus secure credential storage, rate limiting, audit logs, etc.).

